{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>I have not eaten of it in my mourning.</b> From here [we learn] that it is forbidden to an onen." "<b>And I have not removed of it while impure.</b> Whether I am impure and it is pure, or whether I am pure and it is impure (Sifrei). And where was one warned concerning this? ״לֹא תוּכַל לֶאֱכֹל בִּשְׁעָרֶיךָ״ (Deuteronomy 12) — this is eating in impurity, as is stated regarding disqualified consecrated items (ibid. 15): ״בִּשְׁעָרֶיךָ תֹּאכְלֶנּוּ הַטָּמֵא וְהַטָּהוֹר וְגוֹ״ — but this one you may not eat, by [analogy to] the manner of ״eating in your gates״ spoken of in another place (Yevamot 73)." "<b>And I have not given of it to the dead.</b> To make for him a coffin and shrouds." "<b>I have hearkened to the voice of YHWH my Elohim.</b> I brought it to the Temple chosen [for His Name]." "<b>I have done according to all that You commanded me.</b> I rejoiced and caused others to rejoice with it (Sifrei; Ma'aseh Shabbat 5:12)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:28.844294383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}